<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    BTG_DefendStructure - the entrenched-garrison duty assigned by
    LordJob_BTGDefendStructure to the settlement defenders (human guards +
    gestator mechs; humanlike-only nodes gate themselves and no-op for mechs).

    Design intent: a "reverse siege". Defenders fight, sweep their own halls,
    and satisfy every need without ever leaving the structure footprint - there
    is no assault behavior, and nothing (combat, food, rest) can bait them
    outside. Node order IS the behavior spec: ThinkNode_Priority takes the
    first non-null job, so combat sits above ordinary needs and each need sits
    above its own last resort.

    Containment, in brief: every giver that picks a destination bounds it to
    the structure room-rect union (StructureBoundsCache) or to something that
    only exists inside it (medbay bed, comms console, interior blast door),
    and the lord walk grid biases every route interior (+70/cell outside; see
    LordJob_BTGDefendStructure). The one vanilla-unbounded search left is baby
    food, which only spawns inside. Per-giver mechanics and edge cases are
    documented on the giver classes.

    On settlement defeat the lord leaves this duty for the abandon-ship chain
    (BTG_EscapeWalker / BTG_StrandedDefender) - recovered survivors evacuate
    or go peaceful instead of resuming the fight.
  -->

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>BTG_DefendStructure</defName>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <!-- 1. Critically wounded: withdraw out of LoS inside the structure, tend,
             then rejoin. Above combat, and unlike the tend nodes below it fires
             even with hostiles in sight. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGWithdrawAndTend" />
        <!-- 2. Re-arm when unarmed: own downed-drop first (wherever it lies), else
             the nearest decent unreserved weapon in-structure. Above combat -
             fetching a gun is the unarmed defender's combat move. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGRecoverWeapon" />
        <!-- 3. Combat: engage in-structure targets before any ordinary need. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGDefendStructure" />
        <!-- 4. Hunt: no target in sight but a live hostile stands in-structure -
             walk toward the nearest interior-reachable one; the expiring Goto
             hands over to combat the moment sight opens. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGHuntIntrudersInStructure" />
        <!-- 5. Tendable wounds but no Manipulation (self-tend needs it too, so the
             two partition the wounded): lie in a medbay bed for the paramedic.
             Downed pawns are the medic's rescue job, not this node's. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGSeekTreatmentInMedbay" />
        <!-- 6. Self-tend when not in combat (in place; no containment needed). -->
        <li Class="JobGiver_SelfTend" />
        <!-- 7. Childcare during lulls: bottle-feed, then re-crib faction infants
             (same givers the sheltering family uses) - caretaker priority, above
             the defender's own meals. Feed sits above tuck so a hungry stray baby
             is fed in one motion (the feed's finalizer re-cribs it afterwards)
             instead of being tucked and immediately lifted back out to feed. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Civilians.JobGiver_BTGFeedBaby" />
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Civilians.JobGiver_BTGTuckBabyInCrib" />
        <!-- 8. Eat: in-structure food only - carried rations, item food, then the
             last-resort sources (paste valve, meal pallets, dispensers). Never
             corpses, never raw hydroponics produce. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGForageInStructure">
          <minCategory>Hungry</minCategory>
        </li>
        <!-- 9. Starving with nothing left in-structure: call resupply from a comms
             console (meal pod + optional reinforcement raid). Gated one rung past
             the forager so real food is always tried first. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGCallResupply">
          <minCategory>Starving</minCategory>
        </li>
        <!-- 10. Starving and sealed behind a locked blast door: hack the nearest
             one open, then re-evaluate so the food nodes can path. Only interior
             doors exist to hack (the perimeter is VacBarriers). -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGHackDoorForFood">
          <minCategory>Starving</minCategory>
        </li>
        <!-- 11. Rest in-structure. Sleepers rejoin a fight natively: LayDown
             re-checks this tree every 211 ticks and damage wakes the same tick. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.JobGiver_BTGRestInStructure">
          <minRestCategory>Tired</minRestCategory>
        </li>
        <!-- 12. Idle: wander near the focus point. -->
        <li Class="JobGiver_WanderNearDutyLocation">
          <wanderRadius>12</wanderRadius>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
